274:\subsection{Replication check}
275:Before any seeding experiment we replicated each solver against its
276:published results on the twelve classical interval instances. The GA and
277:fEABC replications match the published average relative errors within
278:${\sim}1$ percentage point on all twelve instances (fEABC matches or
279:slightly improves on every one); fEABC-LS reproduces the published ranking
280:(best of its family). Our ABCE3 replication runs systematically
281:${\sim}1.5$--$2.5$ pp above the published averages; we were unable to close
282:this gap from the published description and disclose it here.
284:We take the published parameter settings verbatim, but that is a statement
285:about the configuration, not a claim that our implementation is
286:behaviourally identical to the authors' own. The ABCE3 gap above shows it
287:need not be, and the local-search footnote to Table~\ref{tab:portfolio} shows
288:where the two can diverge while the parameter file reads the same. Neither
289:affects any conclusion of this paper, because every seeding comparison is
290:within-solver: a seeded arm against the unseeded control of the same
291:implementation, under the same budget, on the same instances.
