1558:The failure is therefore the opposite of premature convergence: within a
1559:fixed budget the seeded GA never consolidates. Its control contracts by
1560:$51.0\%$ in structural spread and exploits the region it has found; under
1561:V2 the seeded variant contracts by only $22.7\%$ and is still exploring
1562:when the budget expires. The proximate cause is that the seeds, being
1563:drawn from generators with different construction logic, are good but
1564:mutually \emph{dissimilar}; JOX recombining two structurally divergent
1565:parents produces offspring that inherit the operation ordering of neither,
1566:so selection cannot accumulate structure. The harm grows with instance size
1567:(Section~\ref{sec:res-size}) because longer chromosomes need more
1568:generations to consolidate, and the budget does not grow proportionally.

